 "transcript": [
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Why do you not come in to your father and eat a little food?\"",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"We have been to the officer's house, father, and the house is very fine and the food is very fine and I have a new wife and my brother is very rich and has a great grain market and it is very fine and very pleasant.\"",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung enters, sees his sons.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung scolds eldest son",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Now I would go to the city gate and see the townsfolk if I had a little silver in my hand and I would buy a little meat and I would eat it in my own house and I would eat it when it was hot and I would have my sons eat it too and why should you two eat the cold rice in the shop!\"",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] The eldest son eats cold rice with his brothers.",
  "[says] Wang Lung asks his son about the officer's wife.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Tell me about her face,\"",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son looks at his wife.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung laughs at his son's pride.",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The second son laughs at his father.",
  "the second son (to the eldest son): \"A pretty one she is, to look at, and she could have had a good husband, you and I both know!\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"She is a good and a fair one,\"",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[says] Wang Lung responds to the boy's laughter.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung laughs at his son's laughter.",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son laughs at his father's words.",
  "[action] The eldest son laughs at his father's words."
